/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_Linux
 *
 * Native target presets:
 *
 * @code
 * linux_gcc_x64
 * linux_clang_x64
 * linux_gcc_arm64
 * linux_clang_arm64
 * @endcode
 *
 * Foundation uses Ninja Multi-Config so Debug and Release share one build tree
 * without mixing object files or duplicating installed headers.
 * GCC and Clang are different compatibility targets and therefore use separate
 * presets and distribution directories.
 *
 * These are native presets. The x64 presets require an x86-64 Linux host and the
 * Arm64 presets require an AArch64/Arm64 Linux host. They do not install a
 * cross-compiler or sysroot and will reject a mismatched detected processor.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildLinuxApplication Application Development
 *
 * A Linux application should use the `FetchContent` workflow in
 * @ref Foundation_BuildGuide_Overview. It compiles Foundation with the
 * application's selected GCC or Clang toolchain, so no Foundation export,
 * installation, or `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` is needed while developing. For a
 * single-configuration Ninja application build:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
 * cmake --build build
 * @endcode
 *
 * The host architecture and compiler used to configure the application select
 * the resulting Foundation build. Configure the application separately on x64
 * and Arm64 hosts; these native presets are not cross-compilers.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * gcc --version
 * ninja --version
 * ./scripts/configure.sh linux_gcc_x64 --fresh
 * ./scripts/build.sh linux_gcc_x64 --config Debug --target Foundation
 * ./scripts/build.sh linux_gcc_x64 --config Release --target Foundation
 * ./scripts/export.sh linux_gcc_x64 --fresh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Repeat with the Clang preset after recording `clang++ --version`. Inspect the
 * exported objects with `file`, `readelf`, or `llvm-readobj`, and validate the
 * distributed Release package with an external `find_package` consumer through
 * `Foundation::Foundation`. That package validation is distinct from the
 * `FetchContent` development workflow.
 */
